  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1200 AM CDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nThursday night through Friday will be the most hardest part of \nthe forecast given the uncertainty in the timing and placement of \nthe cold front. The ECMWF and GFS guidance and their ensembles are\nin agreement on sending the front into the Coastal Plains by \nFriday afternoon, but despite the front pushing further south, \nsome lingering convection is expected and with likely saturated \nsoils from Wednesday's and Thursday's rains, additional flooding \nis possible.\n\nFor the weekend, some mid-level energy will remain in place which \nmay spark additional showers and storms each day. The mid to upper \nlevel trough will get stuck over southwest Texas, resulting in those \ncontinued rain and storm chances. By Monday, medium range guidance \nshows cooler and drier weather along with pleasant humidity, \nsomething we've waited months for. Fall is here.",
